		<dc:title id="title">The Duke of York’s Steps</dc:title>
		<meta property="file-as" refines="#title">Duke of York’s Steps, The</meta>
		<dc:subject id="subject-1">Detective and mystery stories</dc:subject>
		<meta property="authority" refines="#subject-1">LCSH</meta>
		<meta property="term" refines="#subject-1">sh85037260</meta>
		<dc:subject id="subject-2">Police--Great Britain--Fiction</dc:subject>
		<meta property="authority" refines="#subject-2">LCSH</meta>
		<meta property="term" refines="#subject-2">sh2008109305</meta>
		<meta property="schema:genre">Mystery</meta>
		<meta id="collection-1" property="belongs-to-collection">Inspector Poole</meta>
		<meta property="collection-type" refines="#collection-1">series</meta>
		<meta property="group-position" refines="#collection-1">1</meta>
		<meta property="schema:abstract">After a wealthy banker’s sudden death is ruled to have been from natural causes, his daughter’s suspicions prompt a detective to take a second look at the case.</meta>
		<dc:description>
			&lt;p&gt;Despite the pleadings of his doctor, family, and friends to consider his aneurysm, Sir Garth Fratten, a wealthy banker, refuses to curtail his work schedule. So it comes as a surprise to no one when he dies suddenly and dramatically on the Duke of York’s Steps—except to Inez, his daughter, who doesn’t accept that he died of natural causes. At her prompting, Detective-Inspector John Poole takes another look, uncovering family secrets and suspicious financial dealings. Could Fratten have been murdered?&lt;/p&gt;
		</dc:description>
